# Without a script to execute and with the summary switched off: the command's first argument is empty, the
# recipient is the configuration's, the summary argument is the alert's name; an entry without a class shows
# Unknown. The table (scripted here) says the alarm was notified as CRITICAL before.
default-exec -
use-summary 0
last-executed CRITICAL
rules tests/corpus/notify/defaults.conf
rules tests/corpus/notify/plain.conf
chart loop.n loop.n_name loop.notify disks things 1
label loop.n kind ssd
var loop.n v 10
clock 0
pass 0
var loop.n v 70
clock 1
pass 1
var loop.n v 10
clock 2
pass 2
